I've known a bunch of people now that breeze through the end game with 
their ring of conflict (at least I have), simply walking past monsters that  
are too busy fighting each other.

Or, facing Demogorgon and wishing for a cockatrice corpse.

I wrote a patch that adds these as conducts. If you use conflict or 
instantly kill a creature (wand of death, disintegration, cockatrice 
corpse, slime or drawbridge) you break the conduct.

http://www.csh.rit.edu/~topher/nethack/addedconducts.diff

The new conducts can be enabled/disabled in config.h

Any feedback on what people think or what can be improved is welcome. 
Something I'm thinking of adding is when both conducts are enabled, 
breaking both of them when a conflict is used to stone a monster with a 
live cockatrice.

